# Conventions + gotchas

## Server vs client components

- **Default to server components.** Mark `"use client"` only when the
  component needs hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useRouter`, etc.).
- Never import server-only modules (`postgres`, `fs`, `net`, `tls`)
  into a client component — Next.js 16 will fail the build with
  cryptic "Module not found" errors.
- Pattern when this happens: split the module into a `-types.ts`
  client-safe twin (see `src/lib/data/field-mappings-types.ts` vs
  `src/lib/data/field-mappings.ts`).

## Mutations: API routes only

- Every write goes through `POST /api/...`. Server components don't
  mutate.
- After a successful mutation, the client calls `router.refresh()` to
  re-fetch server data.
- For collections under concurrent edit (personal-todos, customer
  signals), use the PATCH-ops pattern: client sends a list of
  operations (`add`, `update`, `remove` by id) rather than the full
  collection. Avoids stomping concurrent writes.

## KV store patterns

- Keys are namespaced: `csm:<feature>:v<n>`. Bump the version when
  shape changes.
- `applyOverride(customer, override)` in `src/lib/data/customer-overrides.ts`
  is the canonical merge. Don't bypass it.
- `customer_overrides.field_overrides` is an open bag — new mappable
  fields don't need a dedicated column.

## HubSpot quirks

- Internal property names are lowercase + underscored, sometimes with
  a trailing underscore. Confirmed live names:
  - Stripe customer ID: `stripe_customer_id__saas_` (note trailing `_`)
  - Risk level: `property_risk_level_csm_`
- HubSpot occasionally returns boolean `false` for string-typed
  properties. The mapper coerces every string property through
  `asStringCell()` — keep that pattern when adding new fields.
- `searchCompaniesByStripeIds` in `src/lib/integrations/hubspot.ts`
  is the primary join. `hubspot_company_id` is derived from this, not
  read raw from q10600 anymore.

## Metabase mapper allowlist (CRITICAL)

`src/lib/data/metabase-mapper.ts` silently drops any field not
explicitly listed. When you add a column to a Metabase question OR
add a field to `Customer`, you MUST also add it to the mapper.
Otherwise enrichment passes through but the UI reads `null`.

## Tailwind patterns

- Multi-row sections: prefer `divide-y divide-border/60` over
  `space-y-N` — gives a visual separator and keeps rows aligned.
- Row padding for stacked rows: `py-3 first:pt-0 last:pb-0`.
- Long-form prose: `break-words whitespace-pre-wrap leading-relaxed`.
- Inline edit + value: `inline-flex items-center gap-1.5`.

## Customer helpers

`src/lib/customer-helpers.ts` has shared derivation logic
(`lastContacted`, `subUtilFraction`, etc.). Use these instead of
recomputing — at least four bugs have come from divergent local
implementations.

## Things that have bitten us before

- **React error #418** (hydration mismatch) usually from rendering
  `Date.now()` / locale-formatted dates server-side. Use ISO strings
  on the server and format in the client.
- **Bulk operations silently fail** if `window.confirm()` is
  suppressed by the browser. Use an inline two-step React confirm
  (see `src/components/at-risk-table.tsx` `bulkResolve`) for
  destructive actions.
- **`property_customer_goals: false`** rendering as the literal word
  "false" — fixed by `asStringCell()` in the mapper. Watch for the
  same pattern on any new HubSpot string property.
- **Sub-utilization heuristic** divides `active_subs / max_subscriptions`
  directly. Don't reintroduce the old `> 1 ? /100 : x` heuristic — it
  mis-handled over-cap customers.
